xternalized source ID>\nSOURCE_VERSION: <exact 64-hex version>\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: <exact newly externalized RESULT ID>\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: <one exact unique single-line substring copied from that source inside the delivered result>\nMODE: source_reported_fact or source_reported_relationship\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE or comma-separated exact source IDs named by both the statement and the anchor's containing source line\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: <one complete single-line source-attributed fact or relationship>\n\nThe host, not you, resolves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nCHARTER: 6cb6875c0d4316fa8be25f0b568bd2924e571af7f2cb30e755336344339e5174\nCULTURE: 4afe715ed5a632f384658d45a19fda0c6f1bc5476bc24ab525c75687df9c5d46\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Orchard\nbiologics facility:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Evidence and Decision Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision` and containing exactly these ordered\n   level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and restart states`\n   2. `Process, genealogy, and hold-time controls`\n   3. `Aseptic, analytical, and cold-chain release gates`\n   4. `Utilities, materials, staffing, and staged restart`\n   5. `Cybersecurity, telemetry, and evidence custody`\n   6. `Safety, environmental, and communication continuity`\n   7. `Execution, rollback, and contingencies`\n   8. `Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,400–1,900 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. It must reconcile\nauthority, process performance, aseptic controls, cold-chain excursion,\nutilities, analytical disposition, cybersecurity, materials/staffing,\nenvironmental duties, monitoring, communications, candidate lineage, and\nindependent readiness.\n\nDo not merely list facts. Bind every action and gate to owners, prerequisites,\nobservations, current candidate/version, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that\nretires temporary controls. Preserve exact distinctions including observations\nversus gates, alert versus action limits, installed versus usable capacity,\npercent versus probability, hours versus days, source-local authority, and\ncurrent versus stale evidence.\n\nThe task-native artifacts are exact cumulative work. Checks are candidate-bound\nmechanical feedback and do not independently authorize lot release, commercial\nrestart, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-001 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CHARTER:1-64+CULTURE:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"972dca61657b5271277e7a63647e4420761591b9d38425ccc3dba3a0dee430e9\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CULTURE\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8269}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHARTER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CHARTER_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6cb6875c0d4316fa8be25f0b568bd2924e571af7f2cb30e755336344339e5174\",\"source_size_bytes\":3964,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Restart authority and accountable disposition\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident lead may isolate equipment and order emergency stabilization. Only the independent quality unit may release a manufactured lot, and only the site head may authorize commercial restart after current quality, aseptic, utility, and cyber evidence is reconciled.\nEmergency procurement does not waive validated methods, operator qualification, chain of custody, environmental permits, data-integrity controls, or deviation review. A successful mechanical check is not lot release or commercial restart authority.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving lead acknowledges the same batch genealogy, fill-line configuration, cold-chain map, utility state, and control-system version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nASSAY and STERILE provide release evidence but cannot authorize release; REVIEW provides independent readiness findings but cannot execute restart.\nCHANGE binds candidate lineage while CHARTER preserves separation among stabilization, execution, verification, release, restart authorization, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-lead | v3 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | quality-unit | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | site-head | v3 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | regulatory-liaison | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | 