n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision` and containing exactly these ordered\n   level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and restart states`\n   2. `Process, genealogy, and hold-time controls`\n   3. `Aseptic, analytical, and cold-chain release gates`\n   4. `Utilities, materials, staffing, and staged restart`\n   5. `Cybersecurity, telemetry, and evidence custody`\n   6. `Safety, environmental, and communication continuity`\n   7. `Execution, rollback, and contingencies`\n   8. `Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,400–1,900 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. It must reconcile\nauthority, process performance, aseptic controls, cold-chain excursion,\nutilities, analytical disposition, cybersecurity, materials/staffing,\nenvironmental duties, monitoring, communications, candidate lineage, and\nindependent readiness.\n\nDo not merely list facts. Bind every action and gate to owners, prerequisites,\nobservations, current candidate/version, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that\nretires temporary controls. Preserve exact distinctions including observations\nversus gates, alert versus action limits, installed versus usable capacity,\npercent versus probability, hours versus days, source-local authority, and\ncurrent versus stale evidence.\n\nThe task-native artifacts are exact cumulative work. Checks are candidate-bound\nmechanical feedback and do not independently authorize lot release, commercial\nrestart, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-002 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:STERILE:1-64+CHILL:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"fa24360cb7042daa541a52323934190fec14b1555b2c1cc25a58892636882830\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"STERILE\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CHILL\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7921}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"STERILE\",\"source_path\":\"sources/STERILE_ASEPTIC.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"19a5fe9d20e744fef04763096ac79029de041a7a5b0004926e87761852415188\",\"source_size_bytes\":3468,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Aseptic processing and contamination-control evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe latest media fill found zero contaminated units across 9,600 filled units. Clearance requires three consecutive successful media fills; one clean run is insufficient.\nThe action limit is 1 CFU per cubic meter in Grade A active air, while the alert limit is 3 CFU per plate in the adjacent Grade B settle test. The locations, units, and limit types must not be interchanged.\nA glove, transfer port, sterilization cycle, filling path, viable-air method, or environmental-monitoring plan change makes earlier aseptic evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCULTURE provides batch genealogy, ASSAY consumes sterility evidence, and GUARD constrains validated access to the filling controller.\nCHARTER assigns release authority; STERILE findings alone cannot authorize lot release or restart.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| ASP-000 | filling-line | v3 | 0.0 | cfu | superseded |\n| ASP-001 | isolator | v3 | 1.7 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-002 | transfer-port | v3 | 0.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-003 | environmental-zone | v3 | 2.2 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-004 | filling-line | v3 | 1.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-005 | isolator | v3 | 2.7 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-006 | transfer-port | v3 | 1.5 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-007 | environmental-zone | v3 | 0.3 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-008 | filling-line | v3 | 2.0 | cfu | current |\n| ASP-009 | isolat